# Deploy: Dev first, Prod only on “go to prod”

## Environments (Railway)

| Env | Domain | Git branch |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Dev** | `https://dev.bestie.mx` | `develop` |
| **Prod** | `https://www.bestie.mx` | `main` |

## Default path (every implementation)

1. Work on **`develop`** (or a feature branch that merges into `develop`).
2. After implementing, **commit and push to `develop` only**.
3. Tell the user the change is on **Dev** (`dev.bestie.mx`) and wait for validation.

**Never** push implementation commits directly to `main` / Prod as part of normal prompt work.

## Promote to Prod — only on explicit request

Promote **only** when the user clearly says to ship Prod, e.g.:

- “go to prod”
- “promote to prod”
- “deploy to production”
- “merge develop to main”

Then:

1. Ensure `develop` is clean and contains the intended work.
2. Merge `develop` → `main` (or PR + merge), then `git push origin main`.
3. Confirm Prod (`www.bestie.mx`) will pick up `main`.

If the user did **not** use that kind of language, **do not** push/merge to `main`.

## Forbidden without “go to prod”

- Committing or pushing feature work straight to `main`
- Merging `develop` → `main` “to finish the task”
- Treating `main` as the default deploy target for agent work
- Changing **Prod** Railway (or other host) config during Dev work — see below

## Prod config during Dev work

Do **not** change production infrastructure while only shipping code to Dev. Env var / secret / service / domain changes on **Prod** often **redeploy Prod** and bypass the Dev gate.

| Phase | Allowed |
| --- | --- |
| Working on **`develop` / Dev** | Set or change vars on **bestie-dev** (Dev) only. Document any Prod vars the promote will need (name + value) in the reply — do **not** apply them on Prod yet. |
| User said **go to prod** (or equivalent) | Apply pending Prod config (e.g. `railway variables … --service bestie-prod`), then merge/push `main` (or right after, if the build needs the var). |

Examples that count as Prod config: `VITE_*` / API secrets on **bestie-prod**, scaling, domains, volumes, linking services in the production environment.

If a Prod-only var is required for the feature to work after promote, prepare it in the Dev turn and apply it **only** in the promote step.

## After a mistaken Prod push

If work landed on `main` first, still sync Dev (`merge main → develop` or cherry-pick) and remind the user of this rule for next time.
